# Hala foundations

`styles/foundations.css` is the design system. It is the only source of color, type, spacing, radius, border, shadow, motion, and layout. Import it once at the app root. Every component uses these variables.

Token names match the foundations: `brand/500` is `--brand-500`, `space/4` is `--space-4`, `text/primary` is `--text-primary`.

## Components

Component CSS, HTML, and React `style` values come from `styles/foundations.css` only.

- Color: `--brand-*`, `--text-*`, `--surface-*`, `--status-*`, `--chart-*`, `--gradient-*`
- Space and size: `--space-*`, `--pad-*`, `--gap-*`, `--size-*`, `--icon-*`, `--layout-*`, `--inset-row`
- Radius, border, shadow, motion: `--radius-*`, `--border-*`, `--shadow-*`, `--motion-*`, `--ease-*`, `--focus-ring`
- Type: `--font-*`, `--type-*`, or a `.type-*` class

No hex, `rgb()`, `hsl()`, raw `px` or `rem`, raw `box-shadow`, or font family names in a component. `0` is the only bare length allowed.

A missing value is added to `styles/foundations.css` first. The component then references the new variable.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.card { background: #FFFFFF; padding: 24px; border-radius: 20px; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(12,31,26,.12); }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.card {
  background: var(--surface-card);
  padding: var(--pad-card-y) var(--pad-card-x);
  border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-1);
  color: var(--text-primary);
}
```

```jsx
/* ❌ BAD */
<div style={{ color: "#0C1F1A", padding: 16, borderRadius: 12 }} />

/* ✅ GOOD */
<div style={{ color: "var(--text-primary)", padding: "var(--space-4)", borderRadius: "var(--radius-m)" }} />
```

## Use

- Brand green is for the logo, primary actions, links, focus, and selection. Primary buttons use `var(--gradient-primary)` and `var(--shadow-brand)`.
- Text uses `--text-primary`, `--text-secondary`, `--text-tertiary`, `--text-label`, or `--text-disabled`.
- Status colors are for status only. Pair `--status-success` with `--status-success-tint` and `--status-success-text` (same for warning, error, info, scheduled).
- Amounts, IBANs, dates, and codes use `--font-mono`.
- Arabic uses `--font-arabic`. Do not add letter-spacing to Arabic text.
- Web uses the CSS variables. Android (dp) and iOS (pt) use the same numbers and the same names.
